I agree with .epkat.

In addition (in particular), I believe that the use of ZOI in speech 
is different from it's use in writing.  In speech, it can be used to 
quote non-speech sounds that do not have any representation in speech 
(play a tape of thunder, pages rustling, etc).  In writing, it can be 
used to quote non-lerfu-based visual things (such as pictures ); in 
fact, I came across (long ago) a short story whose "name" was a blot 
- very difficult to add to the short story index I was keeping at the time.

mi'e noras. 



